surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Chappey</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Georges-Courbot</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubreuil</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mauclere</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Simian T-cell lymphotropic virus type 1 from Mandrillus sphinx as a simian counterpart of human T-cell lymphotropic virus type 1 subtype D.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>72</volume><fpage>10316</fpage><lpage>10322</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9811783</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006050-Slattery1"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Slattery</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Franchini</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gessain</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Genomic evolution, patterns of global dissemination, and interspecies transmission of human and simian T-cell leukemia/lymphotropic viruses.</article-title><source>Gen Res</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>525</fpage><lpage>540</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006050-VanDooren1"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Dooren</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Salemi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vandamme</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Dating the origin of the African human T-cell lymphotropic virus type-i (HTLV-I) subtypes.</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>661</fpage><lpage>671</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11264418</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006050-LekanaDouk